Changes log for PCConfig

  v0.61 (11th January 1998)

* Major fiddle to work with multiple configurations in !Boot.Choices.PC.vX.XX
   (i.e. name stringset in main window, buttons rearranged, internals rewired)

* Idiot-proofed Disc Setup window: writables are now display icons (so you
   can only drag 'real' discs to them).

* Replaced annoying !PCFormat app with MkDOSDisc, a CLI tool which !PCConfig
   launches and handles errors for.  This centralises creation of DOS discs in
   a sensible way.  Also Power Users can now use the tool without PCConfig.

* Added priority options to Switching options, and renamed it to 'PC/RISC OS
   relationships' to generalise it a little.

* Added 'Disable floppies' option to Floppy section

* Added NetLinks section to main window to configure newly-hacked PCNE2

* Moved Advanced Configuration from icon bar menu to main window.  Why it ended
   up down there in the first place I'll never know...

  v0.62 (18th January 1998)

* Fixed bug with discs window always showing changed data (*) even if nothing
   changed

* Configuration setting now mirrored in ChooseCfg, so that whatever config you
   chose last in one program is updated in the other.  Coded rather
   inefficiently in parts, but what the hell; nobody'll notice ;-)

  V0.62 (18th January 1998)

  V0.63 (11th March 1998)

* Added 'Launch !PC' button to main window

* Fixed bug whereby setups for new version weren't being correctly created.

  V0.64 (19th March 1998)

* Added TurboDriverBodge option

* Added IncludeVRAM option

  V0.64a (23rd March 1998)

* Fixed TurboDriverBodge option, and now launches cleanly (i.e. saving 
    config behind it).
  
  V0.64b (02nd Apr 1998)

* Added UseWindowFE back in.  Decided that !PCConfig is hideous.

  V0.65 (22nd May 1998)

* Fixed problem where >255 modes caused counting routine to report none.

* Changed display icons in disc window back to writable

* Moved display memory from 'Windows' setup to 'Memory', and renamed to minimum
    display memory since this is what is it now!

* Changed behaviour of 'Save as new' to 'Create new'

* Idiot-proofed disc window, but still not quite perfect; also new 'RISC OS
    size' indicator in Create Disc window.

  V0.70 (9th June 1998)

* Ripped out relics of Nicko's / Ian's old configuration routines (yacc etc.)
    and replaced advanced window with another toolboxy one.

* Took out (another) configuration loading bug re: importing and creating
    new config folders.

* Added SCSI window for configuring ASPI driver, based on Andreas' !ASPISetup

* Got rid of 'Startup' box and merged it into the (retitled) 'Front-end' window

* Added FastVESA / FrameSkip options to display choices box

* Added asterisks to show which items are configurable at run-time

  V0.71 (24th June 1998)

* Added multiple SCSI card support to SCSI window, and 64K ext buffer option

* Fixed Netlinks window loading problem

* Numbers in Config file can be specified in hex (ASPI is by default)

* multicfg re-written a little to stop inefficient and unreliable loads and
    saves; writable icon in main window made display only, Rename button added,
    slightly more RISC OSified all round.

* SCSI ID in disc window allowed up to 32 now

  V0.72a (30th June 1998)

* Fixed 'Last' file always being written as zero (i.e. doesn't remember your
    which was the last config file you edited)

* Sub-config windows now have their associated icons stuck in the top-right
    hand corner.

  V0.73 (13th July 1998)

* Memory window now shows 'real' amount of memory, i.e. VRAM is deducted 
    depending on state of check box.

* Messages changed to fit user guide.

* All windows Wookified.

* Won't automatically import configs; user gets a choice to use default now.

  V0.74 (23rd July 1998)

* Removed UseWindowFE option; now ignored by !PC too due to front-end changes
    making it obsolete.

  V0.75 (14th August 1998)

* Added Floppy0/Floppy1 options back in again

  V0.76 (4th September 1998)

* Added SwitchLFB option 

  v0.80 (1998.12.01)
  
* fettled MKdosdisc so it gets new partitions correct (old one had FAT16
offset from correct position)

  v0.81 (1998.12.04)

* Fettled printing window so that you can't select turbodriver bodge without
  directparallel
    
* Fettled Disc window so that draggin a disc on actually updates the config 

  v0.82 (1999.01.07) 
  
* Put in new SCSI card host recognition code from Andreas 

  v0.83 (1999.01.14)
  
* Added Scaletofit option back in.
* Made Asicoptions options correct
* Added some help text
* Added 'revert to defaults' button

  v0.84 (1999.01.26)
  
* Update from Andreas so that number of SCSI cards is correct (even if you
  have none)
* Latest MKDOSDisc (1999.01.26) that can create new partitions OK.

  v0.85 (2000.02.04)
* Uses 'Last' file in <Choices$dir>.PC now. To match !choosecfg
* Changed directory config is written to from <Boot$Dir>.Choices.PC
   to <Choices$Write>.PC
